{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490162-an-ancient-greek-perspective-on-kindred-mythology","id":1490162,"title":"An ancient Greek Perspective On Kindred Mythology","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-14T12:54:30-07:00","id":1490162,"title":"An ancient Greek Perspective On Kindred Mythology","content":"<i>Disclaimer - In real life, I am not Greek. This is written from the point of view of a 6th Generation Methuselah in my setting who was originally from Thrace. It's always been my feeling that Kindred who are older than 1000 years old would have distinctly different views on Caine, the Book of Nod, and Cainite lore. In my setting, the legends of Caine and Enoch in their modern form appeared 500 years ago, with wildly contradiction accounts. Vampires lie, after all. As always, your Masquerade will vary.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>An ancient Perspective On The Book Of Nod and Cainite Legendry </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Young man, let me make a few things perfectly clear - your understanding of the Book of Nod is a purely </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Christian </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">understanding. However, both the vampiric condition and our eschatology is older than your \u201cCaine\u201d myth. I am over 3000 years old and I was a student of Aristotle, sitting at his feet while concealing my nature. Most assuredly, the Kindred of my time </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>were not christians. </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Your Book of Nod is a Christian invention, written from a Christian perspective. Everything in the Chronicle of Shadows and other Kindred mythologies committed to non-oral media are </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>mythologies. </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Kindred lie, fledgling, and our curse is deeper and more ancient than what can be contained within any mythology.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What is fascinating is that in all the mythology of the Kindred that I have heard from </span></span><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Zhonghu, </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Bharat, Anahuac </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">and many other lands, is that there are always a council of progenitors that usually are 7, or 9, or 13, or 108 and a fallen city where they all dwell or place from which they hail. Aside from that, the myths are varied. Each culture has its own understanding of vampires. Some become culturally aware before the Abrahamic religions, and some after. But Kindred existed in nearly all lands before the rise of the various Yahweh doctrines.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is my feeling that the Kindred curse is terrifying, deep and unfathomable, and that we Kindred construct these myths in order to understand our curse. As a student of Aristotle, I am a materialist. While I have seen much in my three millennia, I have seen nothing that can absolutely convince me of the objective truth of any set of spiritual beliefs, especially since in my travels I have witnessed phenomena that *contradict each other.* I have seen gods in Zimbabwe, Roman Lares, nymphs and fauns, and all measures of wonders. Everything that can be conceived of factually exists. Human wizards have a saying - </span></span><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>truth until paradox. </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They are absolutely correct.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is also one of the reasons why the Sabbat hunt ancients like me. You see, they *know* that their Christian eschatology is just a myth, but can\u2019t bear to accept that truth. So, they hunt down people who are evidence of it, like me.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Because I am feeling generous tonight, let me share with </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>our </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">myth of the Kindred, from the times when I was a Neonate, like you.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Tale of the Children of Orpheus and the exile from the Underworld</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Orpheus was the first Kindred, and Eurydice was the first Wraith. Back when you drew breath, you were told the tale of Orpheus and Eurydice, but were not told the entirety of it.<br /> <br /> When Orpheus quested to find his wife, he found her in the court of Hades. Hades allowed Orpheus and Eurydice to be together, but Orpheus was bade that he must now live as a shade of the dead - supping on emotions and memories, and never invading the sunlit world unless bade by the Furies. For a long time, Orpheus and Eurydice were happy together. As a demigod, he even had children with his beloved.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Indeed, Orpheus had 9 children. I will share the names which you know:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tyrannos, the Chief: He was the eldest of the Orpheans. Skilled in rhetoric, charismatic and enduring, he led the children of Orpheus.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oneirop\u00f3los - The Visionary, the child of dreams. She was always dreaming, and so was regarded to be mad, but also a prophet.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u03a7\u03b1\u03ba\u03af\u03bc or </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hakim the Vizier. He was the oracle amongst the children, and first developed Blood Sorcery. He spent much time among the Persian magi.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Skotia - She who was shadow, who most deeply understood the underworld. She was darkness, and commanded it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Kappadok\u00edou - The sage of the dead. Along with Skotia, he knew the lore of the ghosts and inhabitants of Hades\u2019 realm best, and was also a priest.<br /> <br /> Eros - The son of Ares and Aphrodite, the subject of the myth of Eros and Psyche. Psyche eventually grew old and died, and Eros the godling followed her into the Underworld, and he was welcomed by Orpheus and Hades. Eros was the artist of their tribe, still creating works of beauty to honor his beloved wife and mother. His jealous mother didn't appreciate the fact that he gave up Olympus for her, and had the arrogant boy cursed to remain in the underworld. It is sometimes argued that Eros was the ghost and that Psyche was adopted into the clan of Orpheus, becoming the blood drinker instead.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Logios - The debater. The sage among the children of Orpheus, who challenged Tyrannos at every turn.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lykos - The Wolf. She was a friend of the shapeshifters and went on their hunts.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">S\u00edranges - The Tunneler, who had befriended and then betrayed the furies. Their descendants pursue the tunnelers, hungry for eternal vengeance. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Hydra - he who lurked with the powers of chaos in the depths, he was called The Dragon, and could take any form, or mold others, and was always, always hungry.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">These were the clan names of my time.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Orpheus and Eurydice raised their children in the underworld. They fed from rivers of blood and blood fruits, and never hungered. For creatures such as them, the underworld was paradise.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When Orpheus and his wife sought to leave the underworld, his children followed them. It was appropriate, for unlike their children, Orpheus and Eurydice were man and woman, and were permitted to die a human death. But the 9 had been born in the Underworld, and had walked the Elysian fields and Tartarus. They were not of the sunlight world.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">After consulting with Athena and the Furies, Hades permitted the children to follow their parents. However, Hades bade them not to look back, or they would be cursed. Eurydice did, and was taken back into the underworld, and became the very first Wraith. The children of Orpheus, born in the underworld, had never truly died, and so were undead. They were also demigods, of the 3rd generation from Olympus, being that their father Orpheus was a child of great<br /> Apollo. Terribly, Apollo regarded this as hubris as well - this is why all Orpheans are burned by fire and sunlight, their grandfather Apollo seeking to return them to Hades, who is their true lord.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To stave off the call back to Hades, Orpheans always, always hunger for the blood of living things. They can not sustain themselves on food and drink, and can only take what is offered during sacrifice - blood. However, Hades will have his subjects return, and as they defy the will of the gods, they become more and more monsters, in truth. They are supposed to be dead, and their very existence defies the will of the Olympians.<br /> <br /> Orpheus created a city with his children, meant to be a symposia for all learning, but that is a tale for another time.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The others, such as Ravannah, Sutekh or that 3 eyed sage? They weren\u2019t Greek, so I can\u2019t speak about them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Xerphones of Thrace, 2022 AD, Boston</span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","user":"Robert Armsley","date":".  Edited 9.19.26 - added Toreador analogue 09-19-2026, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T18:24:43-07:00","id":1490205,"title":"","content":"This is a really good take. I have always thought that Judeo-Christian mythology in a time when Jewish religion was a drop of monotheism among an ocean of different politheistic beliefs didn't make any sense. I will definitely use this material for my year 340 BCE chronicle","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T22:25:27-07:00","id":1490216,"title":"","content":"Interesting interpretation.<br /> <br /> I just switched out the Biblical Flood with the Flood of Deucalion of Greek Myth. In terms of the pre-Flood Curse that originated vampirism, I used the dismemberment of Dionysus (Zagreus) by the Titans. That mirrored the basic elements of the mythic origins of vampires in VtM well enough. Before they considered their powers to either be a Curse from God or Blessing of Lilith, it was because they had the Ichor of a god in their veins. <br /> <br /> In my chronicles, while the Book of Nod is pre-dominantly monotheistic myth that formed around 1500 years ago as Christianity displaced the Classical pagan religions, there are plenty of Noddist scholars who incorporate earlier myths in their quest for understanding of their own origins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T23:49:22-07:00","id":1490223,"title":"","content":"That was very interesting and I will probably add that to my list of VtM myths for my chronicles.<br /> <br /> But I have one correction to make: Aristotle lived in the 4th century BC. This Methuselah couldn't be both more than 3 millennia old and a student of Aristotle <i>when alive</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T08:55:18-07:00","id":1490258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490162-an-ancient-greek-perspective-on-kindred-mythology?p=1490205#post1490205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a really good take. I have always thought that Judeo-Christian mythology in a time when Jewish religion was a drop of monotheism among an ocean of different politheistic beliefs didn't make any sense. I will definitely use this material for my year 340 BCE chronicle</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the kind words and validation!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T08:55:49-07:00","id":1490259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490162-an-ancient-greek-perspective-on-kindred-mythology?p=1490223#post1490223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was very interesting and I will probably add that to my list of VtM myths for my chronicles.<br /> <br /> But I have one correction to make: Aristotle lived in the 4th century BC. This Methuselah couldn't be both more than 3 millennia old and a student of Aristotle <i>when alive</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ll make sure to correct that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T09:09:44-07:00","id":1490260,"title":"","content":"In my Greek game, which was short, each of the Clans had a different Greek God patron from the 12 official ones.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T09:27:22-07:00","id":1490262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490162-an-ancient-greek-perspective-on-kindred-mythology?p=1490205#post1490205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a really good take. I have always thought that Judeo-Christian mythology in a time when Jewish religion was a drop of monotheism among an ocean of different politheistic beliefs didn't make any sense. I will definitely use this material for my year 340 BCE chronicle</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't even monotheistic back in the day. There are still a couple of little hints in the bible that the Jewish God used to be a more Zeus-like figure with a wife. It seems to have become a monetheistic religion because the Jews kept getting conquered, which had the effect of simplifying their religion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T16:38:14-07:00","id":1490314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490162-an-ancient-greek-perspective-on-kindred-mythology?p=1490205#post1490205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a really good take. I have always thought that Judeo-Christian mythology in a time when Jewish religion was a drop of monotheism among an ocean of different politheistic beliefs didn't make any sense. I will definitely use this material for my year 340 BCE chronicle</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the creators of VtM was raised by a Lutheran Pastor. A major influence on him, and thus the game, was fear of facing judgment from the Old Testament God, who flooded the world and smote Egypt repeatedly with curses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490162-an-ancient-greek-perspective-on-kindred-mythology?p=1490262#post1490262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wasn't even monotheistic back in the day. There are still a couple of little hints in the bible that the Jewish God used to be a more Zeus-like figure with a wife. It seems to have become a monotheistic religion because the Jews kept getting conquered, which had the effect of simplifying their religion.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you could please point me to anything collaborating that Jehovah may have had a wife, it would be appreceated. This is the first I have ever heard of this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T16:45:24-07:00","id":1490315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.nbcnews.com/id/wbna42154769\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/t_nbcnews-fp-1200-630,f_auto,q_auto:best/MSNBC/Components/Photo/_new/110318-GodsWifePhoto-hmed-1155a.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.nbcnews.com/id/wbna42154769\" target=\"_blank\"> Did God have a wife? Scholar says that he did </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.nbcnews.com/id/wbna42154769\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.nbcnews.com/id/wbna42154769 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> God had a wife, Asherah, whom the Book of Kings suggests was worshiped alongside Yahweh in his temple in Israel, according to an Oxford scholar. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T16:49:30-07:00","id":1490318,"title":"","content":"Shekinah, the Queen of Heaven. The feminine aspect of Jehovah. Though I think by the time of Jesus (and largely after the Babylonian Captivity) she had largely been forgotten by the Jews.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T17:48:59-07:00","id":1490323,"title":"","content":"It does make absolute sense for me that Masquerade's internal mythology would be something based on western european culture that would be familiar to modern Kindred, most of whom will follow one of the Abrahamic religions. I want to do the same treatment for other areas of the world, but that would be a huge project and could never be comprehensive. IMO the best solution is to ideate what a particular Elder or Methuselah thinks based on their background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T06:56:40-07:00","id":1490383,"title":"","content":"If you were a student of Aristotle while you breathed you'd be 2300 ish years left, not over 3,000","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T14:10:56-07:00","id":1490653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490162-an-ancient-greek-perspective-on-kindred-mythology?p=1490383#post1490383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you were a student of Aristotle while you breathed you'd be 2300 ish years left, not over 3,000</div> </div> </div> </div>Corrected <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T15:12:55-07:00","id":1490657,"title":"","content":"When I ran vtm rome i ran that claim to be survivors of the golden race under Greek mythology.<br /> <br /> By contrast the neoplatonics associated kindred with simply a misbalance of matter over spirit and mind in a human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T14:00:33-07:00","id":1490736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Armsley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490162-an-ancient-greek-perspective-on-kindred-mythology#post1490162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, Orpheus had 9 children. I will share the names which you know:<br /> <br /> The others, such as Ravannah, Sutekh or that 3 eyed sage? They weren\u2019t Greek, so I can\u2019t speak about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I interpret the names of the 9 children correctly, you did not include the Toreador. You only have 12 clans, not thirteen. Is there a reason you left them out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T10:45:08-07:00","id":1490902,"title":"","content":"This makes me think they would see themselves as Fauns, Nymphs, Furies, Gorgons... you know, agents of the Gods. Even if just in name and can't really... &quot;prove&quot; anything. Which never was important... But the lack of documents and artifacts is kind of weird, there is only NOD.<br /> <br /> I think the Kindred of then would be something that remind me of the Wan Kuei, except that these were golden heroes and guardians for the Gods, and have fallen. So I don't know if Kindred would think themselves as such (fallen). I believe the Titans would be either the origin of Werewolves, or the Baali, or whatever &quot;I don't like it&quot; category. <br /> <br /> I also think at that time, the Clans weren't as well established as they were. Like, there could be two Ventrue cities and a Malkavian one, and one of the Ventrue's could see themselves more closely to the Malks than the other Ventrue. It would be much more provincial I think, more Lineages than Clans. Maybe 'Clans' at the time were really just a bunch of Lineages under a bigger umbrella, so Toreador, Lasombra and Brujah bloodlines could be unite under a single clan name. I don't know... I think its fun to change the entire social and cultural system and structure when you are going very far from what is the norm. <br /> <br /> The only thing I remember well, is that Collat from the later Roman Ventrue was kind of the first dude to think &quot;better to rule from the shadows guys&quot;. So everyone was &quot;hey, I'm god, give me blood&quot; in their way of thinking. I don't remember Menele and Helene's feud enough, but I imagine Troy could've been an even earlier Carthage situation. A Dream City, like so many in Kindred history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T15:16:31-07:00","id":1491127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490162-an-ancient-greek-perspective-on-kindred-mythology?p=1490902#post1490902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes me think they would see themselves as Fauns, Nymphs, Furies, Gorgons... you know, agents of the Gods. Even if just in name and can't really... &quot;prove&quot; anything. Which never was important... But the lack of documents and artifacts is kind of weird, there is only NOD.<br /> <br /> I think the Kindred of then would be something that remind me of the Wan Kuei, except that these were golden heroes and guardians for the Gods, and have fallen. So I don't know if Kindred would think themselves as such (fallen). I believe the Titans would be either the origin of Werewolves, or the Baali, or whatever &quot;I don't like it&quot; category.<br /> <br /> I also think at that time, the Clans weren't as well established as they were. Like, there could be two Ventrue cities and a Malkavian one, and one of the Ventrue's could see themselves more closely to the Malks than the other Ventrue. It would be much more provincial I think, more Lineages than Clans. Maybe 'Clans' at the time were really just a bunch of Lineages under a bigger umbrella, so Toreador, Lasombra and Brujah bloodlines could be unite under a single clan name. I don't know... I think its fun to change the entire social and cultural system and structure when you are going very far from what is the norm.<br /> <br /> The only thing I remember well, is that Collat from the later Roman Ventrue was kind of the first dude to think &quot;better to rule from the shadows guys&quot;. So everyone was &quot;hey, I'm god, give me blood&quot; in their way of thinking. I don't remember Menele and Helene's feud enough, but I imagine Troy could've been an even earlier Carthage situation. A Dream City, like so many in Kindred history.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It makes sense to me. VTM is choc a bloc with unreliable narrators. Why would good christian Sabbat and Camarilla want to spread heathen lies? Modern kindred are monsters, not archaeologists. And the real ancients, like the Inconnu, are going to speak to the children in a nomenclature they understand.<br /> <br /> From a game design perspective, working from a gothic horror base which uses the dark side of victorian morality as it's base makes sense. This potential hole doesnt really affect the setting, because most of the time you are playing modern Kindred raised in a predominanty christian society as humans. Requiem is more open on this issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T15:18:42-07:00","id":1491128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490162-an-ancient-greek-perspective-on-kindred-mythology?p=1490736#post1490736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I interpret the names of the 9 children correctly, you did not include the Toreador. You only have 12 clans, not thirteen. Is there a reason you left them out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because when I made this it was tough for me to find a paralell from grecian myth. ICly, the narrator may have chosen to leave them out. Also note that his muth doesnt include Salubri or Setites.<br /> <br /> Xerphones is a contemporary to Critias, and in my game they visit every few years to curse at each other in various ancient Greek dialects. Critias might tell a different story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T16:36:08-07:00","id":1492722,"title":"","content":"I have a \u201cCthulhu Mythos cannibal-genesis\u201d for the Kindred. It\u2019s...gruesome. In it, there\u2019s no Caine or 2nd Generation. The Antediluvians weren\u2019t even human, being far older monsters than modern Cainites are willing to accept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T01:07:01-07:00","id":1492963,"title":"","content":"I hope I'm not overly pessimistic but its clear that its a Thracian who has been influenced by ancient Greece and not an ancient Hellene that is talking for the OP PoV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-14T10:04:38-07:00","id":1493065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490162-an-ancient-greek-perspective-on-kindred-mythology?p=1492963#post1492963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope I'm not overly pessimistic but its clear that its a Thracian who has been influenced by ancient Greece and not an ancient Hellene that is talking for the OP PoV.</div> </div> </div> </div>Xerphones is indeed a Thracian! But he's spent centuries in places like Athens and Corinth that he's tired of correcting Kindred who can barely find Rome on a map.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-14T21:10:33-07:00","id":1493095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Armsley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490162-an-ancient-greek-perspective-on-kindred-mythology?p=1493065#post1493065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Xerphones is indeed a Thracian! But he's spent centuries in places like Athens and Corinth that he's tired of correcting Kindred who can barely find Rome on a map.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the confirmation. The idea that he wouldn't go into detail to explain something of which he don't know much was kind of telling that he wasn't a Greek at heart. :P<br /> <br /> As for his attitude to the Greeks, I'll just leave it alone.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-16T10:17:19-07:00","id":1493166,"title":"","content":"I must say I like the thought and care you put into this thread at coming up with different origins for the various clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T22:14:59-07:00","id":1493303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490162-an-ancient-greek-perspective-on-kindred-mythology?p=1493095#post1493095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for the confirmation. The idea that he wouldn't go into detail to explain something of which he don't know much was kind of telling that he wasn't a Greek at heart. :P<br /> <br /> As for his attitude to the Greeks, I'll just leave it alone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One of the ironies around Joseph/Xerphones is that he's now an ancient greek culturally, since he's spent much much more time masquerading as a Greek than as a Thracian. Of course, mosty modern North American Kindred don't know the difference. Ah, the vicissitudes(!) of being an ancient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T18:50:33-07:00","id":1564202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490162-an-ancient-greek-perspective-on-kindred-mythology?p=1490736#post1490736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I interpret the names of the 9 children correctly, you did not include the Toreador. You only have 12 clans, not thirteen. Is there a reason you left them out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Resurrecting this thread -<br /> <br /> I'll see if I can create some kind of analogue. Xerphones does have contemporaries like Menele, Helena and Critias, and Helena won't take kindly to being told her clan doesn't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","user":"Robert Armsley","date":". 09-19-2026, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-20T11:13:47-07:00","id":1564220,"title":"","content":"Nice write up, OP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T15:51:35-07:00","id":1564255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Armsley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490162-an-ancient-greek-perspective-on-kindred-mythology#post1490162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The others, such as Ravannah, Sutekh or that 3 eyed sage? They weren\u2019t Greek, so I can\u2019t speak about them.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming that Sutekh is supposed to be Set, you might draw upon the mythological Typhon as an explanation.<br /> <br /> Specifically the part where he was so borderline unstoppable, that the gods had to flee to Egypt to escape his wrath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-16T10:41:51-07:00","id":1564788,"title":"","content":"I've dropped some mentions of alternate myths to kindred origins in my chronicles through the years - my current one even has <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Critias\" target=\"_blank\">Critias</a> as one of the leaders of a gehenna cult centered around <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timaeus_(dialogue)\" target=\"_blank\">Atlantis </a>and the semi-divine children of Poseidon that founded it as the origin of the kindred, among other things.<br /> <br /> (He also takes the role of Vitel - that in my bizarro continuity, never exposed for secret ties to the Sabbat and still is the prince of Washington - in my version of the events described in BJD)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-17-2026, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}